<%# Shared curl example of every district's labs. Include it with the curl view (see curlFor in districts/_shared/curl.ts); a view with signIn false is for a lab with no sign-in. Every value goes through the escaped output tag. Never put an EJS tag inside an EJS comment: it breaks parsing. %>
<p class="lab-note">From a terminal: <code>curl<% if (curl.method) { %> -X <%= curl.method %><% } %> "<%= curl.url %>"<% curl.headers.forEach(function (h) { %> -H "<%= h %>"<% }); %> -b "hvwa_sid=&lt;copy from devtools&gt;<% curl.cookies.forEach(function (c) { %>; <%= c %><% }); %>"<% if (curl.data) { %> -d '<%= curl.data %>'<% } %><% curl.form.forEach(function (f) { %> --data-urlencode '<%= f %>'<% }); %><% (curl.multipart || []).forEach(function (m) { %> -F '<%= m %>'<% }); %></code>.<% if (curl.multipart && curl.multipart.length) { %> Here <code>filename</code> is the name the server receives and <code>type</code> the content type you claim; curl sends exactly what you write.<% } %> Your lab belongs to your browser session: <% if (curl.signIn === false) { %>open this page in your browser<% } else { %>sign in here first<% } %>, then copy the (HttpOnly) <code>hvwa_sid</code> cookie from the devtools storage into <code>-b</code>. Without it curl starts a different session, and its state and flags will not match yours. The line is bash syntax (Git Bash, WSL, macOS, Linux); in Windows PowerShell write <code>curl.exe</code>, because plain <code>curl</code> there is <code>Invoke-WebRequest</code>.</p>
